/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T21:57:57Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T22:06:59Z","body":"@AdelynneBrito Thanks for investigating, but that doesn't seem necessary.\n\n@clayjohn Is right, this initialization check was only necessary for CanvasItemMaterial. Other Material Classes inherit the initialization methods from the BaseMaterial class, but don't interact with it, and it seems unnecessary?\n\nMy PR: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109369 added `ERR_FAIL_COND_V(!p_from->_is_initialized(), Ref<ShaderMaterial>());` to all of the conversion plugins\n\nThis commit: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/084783e92b829aac3e45ea56741bebff27450556 moved that all to a single location because the behavior was consistent across all conversion plugins.\n\nMy fix suggestion: Move the initialization check from the generic `Ref<ShaderMaterial> MaterialEditor::make_shader_material` back to just being inside `Ref<Resource> CanvasItemMaterialConversionPlugin::convert`\n\nA quick test I did: Rebuilt master with the initialization check removed from Make_Shader_Material, created a new project, created one of every [Shader]Material Resource. Used the conversion plugin on each one. Only CanvasItemMaterial actually failed, every other conversion succeeded as intended.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618730840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"per